Owner: DAVIN. Milestone: M0 §4.5 (auth/dal.ts). Blocked by MF-T05, MF-T06 and MF-T35.

**Binding contract, agreed with ADIT on 2026-11-08 (ADIT's MF-T18 dashboard shell codes against it); don't change it without telling ADIT and ALAN:**
```ts
// apps/web/lib/auth/permissions.ts
export const PERMISSION_KEYS = [/* the 23 catalog keys */] as const;
export type PermissionKey = (typeof PERMISSION_KEYS)[number];

// apps/web/lib/auth/dal.ts ('server-only'); call only inside a <Suspense> boundary
export type CurrentUser = { id: string; email: string };
export function getCurrentUser(): Promise<CurrentUser | null>;          // 'use cache: private'; verified JWT (getClaims/getUser), never getSession
export function requireUser(next?: string): Promise<CurrentUser>;       // redirect('/login?next=…') when signed out

export type OrgStatus = 'active' | 'suspended' | 'past_due' | 'read_only';
export type OrgContext = {
  org: { id: string; slug: string; name: string; status: OrgStatus; currency: string; timezone: string };
  membership: { roleKey: string; roleName: string; allLocations: boolean };
  permissions: PermissionKey[];                  // from my_permissions(org); [] for a suspended org
  locations: { id: string; name: string }[];     // only locations the user can access (has_location_access)
  package: { code: string; name: string; features: string[]; limits: Record<string, number | null> } | null;
};
export function getOrgContext(orgSlug: string): Promise<OrgContext | null>;   // null = not an active member (or unknown slug)
export function requireOrgContext(orgSlug: string): Promise<OrgContext>;      // notFound() when null; same response for unknown org and non-member
export function requirePermission(orgId: string, perm: PermissionKey): Promise<void>; // re-checks has_permission in the DB; forbidden() (403) when missing
export function requirePlatformAdmin(): Promise<CurrentUser>;                  // notFound() unless is_platform_admin()
export function hasFeature(ctx: OrgContext, key: string): boolean;
```
- 404 vs 403: `requireOrgContext` → `notFound()`; `requirePermission` → `forbidden()` from next/navigation. If the installed Next 16 needs a config flag for `forbidden()` (check node_modules/next/dist/docs; it was `experimental.authInterrupts` in 15), enable it in next.config.ts in this PR and note it. Otherwise throw a typed `ForbiddenError` that the dashboard error boundary renders as 403, and tell ADIT which you chose.
- Suspended org: getOrgContext still returns the context (status 'suspended', permissions []) so the layout can show the notice page; every requirePermission fails.
- Location URLs: the dashboard uses `/[org]/[location]/…` with the location **id** (uuid) for location-scoped pages; org-level pages (staff, settings, customers) live at `/[org]/…`. A location id not in ctx.locations → notFound().

Caching: cache keyed by user id + org id, cacheTag `org:{orgId}` and `member:{userId}:{orgId}`, no emails/tokens in keys or tags. A plain `'use cache'` scope cannot read cookies(), so if needed use `'use cache: private'`. **Do not** switch to the service-role client to make caching work; dashboard tenant reads stay under RLS. Note which you chose in the PR.

Rules: org id always derived from the slug + membership, never from client input. JSDoc on each export saying callers must be inside <Suspense>. Vitest unit tests with a mocked Supabase client for every branch. lib/auth/tags.ts: tag helpers for updateTag in Server Actions.

Owner: **ADIT** (moved from DAVIN on 2026-11-08 with the user's approval; a one-time ownership exception covering lib/arcjet.ts, lib/posthog/ and the Arcjet wiring in proxy.ts). Milestone: M0 §4.5. Do this BEFORE MF-T12: DAVIN's MF-T13 (auth actions) uses these presets.

**Binding contract for DAVIN's MF-T13/T15/T17 (pinned 2026-11-08):**
```ts
// apps/web/lib/arcjet.ts ('server-only')
export type ProtectReason = 'RATE_LIMITED' | 'BOT' | 'SHIELD' | 'EMAIL_INVALID';
export type ProtectResult = { allowed: true } | { allowed: false; reason: ProtectReason };
export const ajAuth: ArcjetPreset;        // login / password reset: shield + bot detection + IP rate limit
export const ajSignup: ArcjetPreset;      // shield + bot + rate limit + email validation (disposable / invalid / no MX)
export const ajPublicForm: ArcjetPreset;  // storefront forms (later)
export const ajProbe: ArcjetPreset;       // probe endpoints: checkSlug, getInvitationPreview (tighter rate limit)
// Usable from Server Actions (reads request headers via next/headers); `email` only for ajSignup.
export function protect(preset: ArcjetPreset, opts?: { email?: string }): Promise<ProtectResult>;

// apps/web/lib/posthog/events.ts
export const EVENTS = { signupStarted: 'signup_started', signupCompleted: 'signup_completed', onboardingCompleted: 'onboarding_completed',
  trialStarted: 'trial_started', staffInvited: 'staff_invited', invitationAccepted: 'invitation_accepted', orgStatusChanged: 'org_status_changed' } as const;
// apps/web/lib/posthog/server.ts ('server-only'); flushes via after(), never throws, no-op without keys
export function captureServer(event: (typeof EVENTS)[keyof typeof EVENTS],
  opts: { distinctId: string; organizationId?: string; properties?: Record<string, string | number | boolean | null> }): void;
// apps/web/lib/posthog/client.tsx ('use client'): <PostHogProvider> (identify by user id only, group = organization)
```

Build:
- Arcjet: one shared base (shield + bot detection) and the presets above. DRY_RUN in development unless ARCJET_KEY is set; LIVE in production. `protect()` maps Arcjet decisions to ProtectResult. If ARCJET_KEY is missing in dev, protect() returns allowed:true and logs once.
- Wire Arcjet shield into apps/web/proxy.ts for public and auth routes only; /api/webhooks/doku stays excluded (CLAUDE.md Security). Keep DAVIN's host routing untouched.
- PostHog: events only from EVENTS; groups = { organization: orgId }; **no PII in properties** (no emails, names, phones, tokens); `sanitizeUrl()` used in `before_send` / pageview capture: `/invite/{token}` → `/invite/[token]`, and `token_hash`, `token`, `code`, `next` query params stripped.
- Unit tests: event names snake_case; preset shapes; protect() mapping; sanitizeUrl cases.

Owner: **ADIT** (moved from DAVIN on 2026-11-08 with the user's approval; a one-time ownership exception for lib/email/). Milestone: M0 §4.5 (email/). Do it after MF-T08. Depends on MF-T06 (env, merged) and MF-T11 (StaffInvite template, merged). DAVIN's MF-T17 (staff actions) calls sendStaffInvite.

**Binding contract for DAVIN's MF-T17:**
```ts
// apps/web/lib/email/send.ts ('server-only')
export function send(input: { to: string; subject: string; react: React.ReactElement; from?: string; replyTo?: string;
  idempotencyKey: string; tags?: { name: string; value: string }[] }): Promise<{ ok: boolean; id?: string; error?: string }>; // never throws
// apps/web/lib/email/staff-invite.ts ('server-only')
export function sendStaffInvite(input: { organizationId: string; invitationId: string; sendCount: number; to: string;
  props: StaffInviteProps; replyTo?: string | null }): Promise<{ ok: boolean; id?: string; error?: string }>;
```

Build apps/web/lib/email/ (import 'server-only'), per CLAUDE.md "Email (Resend)":
- `client.ts`: Resend SDK client from serverEnv.RESEND_API_KEY.
- `send.ts`: EMAIL_DELIVERY=log → render to text and console.log (recipient masked, e.g. o***@demo.local), no network. Resend mode passes the idempotency key. Never throws; failures are logged without the API key or body.
- `sendStaffInvite`: sender `"{Restaurant} via Restomate" <orders@mail.restomate.app>` with the restaurant name sanitised (strip quotes, angle brackets, newlines); idempotency key `staff-invite/{invitationId}/{sendCount}`; only passes an acceptUrl starting with `${NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL}/invite/` and an https logoUrl (else null); props.timeZone = the org timezone.
- Callers run sends in `after()`, so the main action never waits or fails on email (JSDoc).
- Vitest: log mode output; header injection neutralised; URL scheme guards; idempotency key format; errors don't throw.

Owner: DAVIN. Milestone: M0 §4.7 (backend half). Blocked by MF-T03 (RPCs) and MF-T07 (DAL). ADIT builds the wizard (MF-T16) against this contract in parallel.

**Binding contract (final, agreed with ADIT 2026-11-08; supersedes the earlier FormData version); don't change it without telling ADIT and ALAN:**
```ts
// apps/web/lib/onboarding/schemas.ts: Zod schemas for each step + the combined OnboardingInput, shared by wizard and action
export type OnboardingInput = {
  name: string; slug: string;
  location: { name: string; address: string; city: string; phone: string; timezone: string; currency: string;
              taxRateBps: number; serviceChargeBps: number; taxOnServiceCharge: boolean };
  branding: { primaryColor: string | null; logoUrl: string | null } | null;
};
// apps/web/lib/onboarding/slug.ts (pure, client-safe)
export function suggestSlug(name: string): string;
// apps/web/lib/onboarding/actions.ts ('use server')
export function checkSlug(slug: string): Promise<{ status: 'available' | 'taken' | 'reserved' | 'invalid' }>;
export function createOrganization(input: OnboardingInput): Promise<ActionResult>;
//   ActionResult from lib/auth/schemas.ts. On success it calls redirect(`/${slug}`) server-side (never returns ok:true);
//   it only returns { ok:false, fieldErrors?, formError? }. Field error keys use dotted paths, e.g. 'slug', 'location.taxRateBps'.
```

Build:
- schemas: name 2–80; slug matching the DB check `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{1,38}[a-z0-9]$`; location.name required, address/city/phone optional (empty string allowed → null); timezone from an allowed IANA list (default Asia/Jakarta); currency 'IDR' | 'USD' (default IDR); taxRateBps / serviceChargeBps integers 0–2500; branding.logoUrl https:// only, ≤ 500 chars; primaryColor `#rrggbb`.
- `checkSlug` via is_slug_available (+ reserved_slugs check for the 'reserved' status, format check for 'invalid'); Arcjet rate limit (it's a probe endpoint).
- `suggestSlug`: lowercase, ascii-fold Indonesian diacritics, hyphens, trimmed to 40.
- `createOrganization`: requireUser; re-validate the whole input with Zod (never trust the client); call the create_organization RPC with branding `{ logo_url, primary_color }` (never pass organization_id, role or price); map SLUG_TAKEN / SLUG_RESERVED → fieldErrors.slug, ORG_LIMIT_REACHED / PLAN_LIMIT:* / INVALID_* → friendly errors; capture onboarding_completed + trial_started (group = new org id, no PII); updateTag for the user's memberships; redirect.
- Vitest: schemas, suggestSlug, error mapping.

Owner: DAVIN. Milestone: M0 §4.8 (backend half). Blocked by MF-T04 (triggers), MF-T07 (DAL) and MF-T12 (email). ADIT builds the pages (MF-T19) against this contract in parallel.

**Binding contract (final, agreed with ADIT 2026-11-08); don't change it without telling ADIT and ALAN.** Every mutation is a **form action** (useActionState shape) with `orgSlug` **bound server-side as the first argument** (`inviteStaff.bind(null, slug)` in the page). **No organization id ever travels in FormData**; the org is derived from the slug + membership (CLAUDE.md).
```ts
// apps/web/lib/staff/data.ts ('server-only')
export type StaffMember = { memberId: string; userId: string; fullName: string | null; email: string | null;
  roleId: string; roleKey: string; roleName: string; status: 'active' | 'deactivated'; allLocations: boolean; locationIds: string[]; isSelf: boolean };
export type StaffInvitation = { id: string; email: string; roleId: string; roleName: string; allLocations: boolean; locationIds: string[];
  expiresAt: string /* ISO */; status: 'pending' | 'expired' };
export type StaffRole = { id: string; key: string; name: string; isSystem: boolean };
export function listStaff(orgSlug: string): Promise<{ members: StaffMember[]; invitations: StaffInvitation[]; roles: StaffRole[]; locations: { id: string; name: string }[]; viewerIsOwner: boolean }>;
//   calls requireOrgContext + requirePermission('staff.manage') itself. Never returns token_hash.

// apps/web/lib/staff/actions.ts ('use server'); ActionResult from lib/auth/schemas.ts (includes the optional `code`, see MF-T13)
type StaffAction = (orgSlug: string, prev: ActionResult | null, formData: FormData) => Promise<ActionResult>;
export const inviteStaff: StaffAction;        // formData: email, roleId, allLocations ('true'|'false'), locationIds (repeated)
export const resendInvitation: StaffAction;   // formData: invitationId
export const revokeInvitation: StaffAction;   // formData: invitationId
export const changeMemberRole: StaffAction;   // formData: memberId, roleId
export const setMemberLocations: StaffAction; // formData: memberId, allLocations, locationIds (repeated)
export const deactivateMember: StaffAction;   // formData: memberId
export const reactivateMember: StaffAction;   // formData: memberId
export function acceptInvitation(prev: ActionResult | null, formData: FormData): Promise<ActionResult>; // formData: token; redirect(`/${slug}`) on success
export function getInvitationPreview(token: string): Promise<{ restaurantName: string; roleName: string; emailHint: string; expired: boolean } | null>;
```
Error codes (in `ActionResult.code`, with a user-friendly `formError`): `PLAN_LIMIT` (staff limit → the UI shows an upgrade prompt), `LAST_OWNER`, `SYSTEM_ROLE`, `ALREADY_INVITED` ("Already invited, use Resend"), `INVALID_INVITATION` (generic), `FORBIDDEN`.

Build apps/web/lib/staff/:
- Every action: requireOrgContext(orgSlug) → requirePermission(org.id, 'staff.manage') → Zod → mutation → audit log → updateTag `org:{orgId}` / `member:*`. Validate that memberId / invitationId / roleId / locationIds belong to that org (IDOR).
- `inviteStaff`: the owner role only if the actor is owner; 32 random bytes (base64url) generated server-side, only the SHA-256 hash stored; sendStaffInvite in after() with acceptUrl `${APP_URL}/invite/{rawToken}` and the org timezone; staff_invited captured (no email in properties).
- `resendInvitation`: rotates the token (new hash, new expiry, send_count + 1), sends again. `revokeInvitation`.
- Member changes: map LAST_OWNER; a user can't change their own role (the DB also blocks self-scope changes for non-owners).
- `acceptInvitation`: requireUser; accept_invitation RPC; generic INVALID_INVITATION on any failure; invitation_accepted captured.
- `getInvitationPreview`: get_invitation_preview RPC with the normal server client (never service role); Arcjet rate limit.
- Vitest: token generation/hash, Zod, error mapping, permission checks with a mocked DAL.

Owner: **ADIT** (moved from DAVIN on 2026-11-08 with the user's approval; a one-time ownership exception for lib/public, lib/storefront, lib/theme.ts and lib/supabase/anon.ts). Milestone: M0 §4.9 (pricing + storefront data). Used by ADIT's own MF-T21 pages (PR #28). Do it after MF-T10.

**Binding contract (unchanged):**
```ts
// apps/web/lib/public/packages.ts
export type PublicPackage = { code: string; name: string; description: string | null; currency: string;
  priceMonthly: number; priceYearly: number; trialDays: number; limits: Record<string, number | null>; features: string[]; isDefault: boolean };
export function getPublicPackages(): Promise<PublicPackage[]>; // is_active && is_public; order by sort_order, then priceMonthly
// apps/web/lib/storefront/get-storefront.ts
