Owner: DAVIN. Milestone: M2 §6 (venue, backend part 2). Needs MVM-T01 (schema). ADIT builds the pages (MVM-T04) against this contract in parallel.

**Binding contract (pinned 2026-11-09; don't change it without telling ADIT and ALAN):** every mutation is a form action (useActionState shape) with `orgSlug` and `locationId` **bound server-side** (`createArea.bind(null, slug, locationId)`). No organization id ever travels in FormData; the org comes from the slug + membership, and the location must belong to it and be accessible to the user.
```ts
// apps/web/lib/venue/data.ts ('server-only')
export type Area = { id: string; name: string; sortOrder: number; isActive: boolean; tableCount: number };
export type VenueTable = { id: string; areaId: string; label: string; capacity: number; shape: 'square' | 'round' | 'rect';
  status: 'available' | 'reserved' | 'occupied' | 'needs_cleaning'; posX: number | null; posY: number | null; isActive: boolean };
export function getVenue(orgSlug: string, locationId: string): Promise<{
  areas: Area[]; tables: VenueTable[]; canManage: boolean; tableLimit: { used: number; max: number | null } }>;
//   requireOrgContext + location access check; any member with access can read; canManage = has tables.manage. Never returns qr_token.
export function getTableQrTokens(orgSlug: string, locationId: string, tableIds?: string[]): Promise<{ tableId: string; label: string; areaName: string; url: string }[]>;
//   tables.manage only; url = `${storefront origin for the org}/t/{qr_token}`; used by the QR print sheet; never cached with a token in the key.

// apps/web/lib/venue/actions.ts ('use server'); ActionResult from lib/auth/schemas.ts
type VenueAction = (orgSlug: string, locationId: string, prev: ActionResult | null, formData: FormData) => Promise<ActionResult>;
export const createArea: VenueAction;      // name
export const renameArea: VenueAction;      // areaId, name
export const setAreaActive: VenueAction;   // areaId, active ('true'|'false'); deactivating an area with active tables -> code AREA_NOT_EMPTY
export const reorderAreas: VenueAction;    // areaIds (repeated, full order)
export const createTable: VenueAction;     // areaId, label, capacity, shape
export const updateTable: VenueAction;     // tableId, areaId, label, capacity, shape
export const setTableActive: VenueAction;  // tableId, active
export const saveTablePositions: VenueAction; // positions = JSON [{tableId, posX, posY}] (Zod-validated, ints 0..999, ≤ 500 items)
export const rotateTableQr: VenueAction;   // tableId -> calls rotate_table_qr_token
```
Error codes added to `ActionErrorCode`: `PLAN_LIMIT` (max_tables → upgrade prompt), `DUPLICATE_NAME` (area name / table label taken), `AREA_NOT_EMPTY`, `FORBIDDEN`.

Build: requireOrgContext → location check → requirePermission('tables.manage') → Zod → write → updateTag (`venue:{locationId}`) → PostHog `area_created`, `table_created`, `table_qr_rotated` (no PII). Validate that every id belongs to that org and location (IDOR). Vitest: Zod, error mapping, permission checks with a mocked DAL.

Owner: REYKI. Pairs with MVM-T06 (DAVIN, PR #73). Write against MVM-T06's acceptance criteria, independently of DAVIN's tests, in supabase/tests/isolation/:
- the read matrix for all 8 menu tables (owner, manager, cashier, waiter, kitchen, location-scoped staff, other org, anon, platform admin);
- cross-tenant writes and cross-org links (category, group or station from another org or location);
- price tampering: a cashier or waiter writing base_price, price_override or sold_out_until directly;
- set_item_sold_out: permission, location scope, other org, inactive item, and the end-of-day boundary in the location's timezone;
- get_public_menu (anon): suspended org, inactive location, unpublished, inactive or sold-out items, unknown slug, and no internal fields.
